{"n":16,"title":"The quiet ones","blurb":"Comparatives and superlatives; describing character","steps":[{"stage":"Warm-up","type":"pick","title":"Read each pair. Click the one that is more true for you.","sub":"Здесь нет правильного ответа","options":[{"label":"I talk to everybody"},{"label":"I stay with the two I know"},{"label":"I say it immediately"},{"label":"I think, then I say it"},{"label":"I go out and see people"},{"label":"I go home and close the door"},{"label":"in a group, out loud"},{"label":"alone, in a quiet room"},{"label":"I answer it"},{"label":"I let it ring and send a message"}]},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"cards","title":"Слова урока","sub":"Нажми на карточку, чтобы увидеть перевод","words":[{"en":"confident","pos":"adj","ru":"уверенный в себе","kk":"өзіне сенімді","def":"sure about your own ability, and not afraid to speak or act","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-confident.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/39a449bf0e1b.mp3"},{"en":"shy","pos":"adj","ru":"застенчивый","kk":"ұялшақ","def":"nervous and uncomfortable with people you do not know","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-shy.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/df399330d331.mp3"},{"en":"sociable","pos":"adj","ru":"общительный","kk":"көпшіл","def":"enjoying being with other people","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-sociable.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/a396870703a9.mp3"},{"en":"friendly","pos":"adj","ru":"дружелюбный","kk":"достық ниетті","def":"kind and pleasant towards other people","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-friendly.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/41209342f361.mp3"},{"en":"hard-working","pos":"adj","ru":"трудолюбивый","kk":"еңбекқор","def":"putting a lot of effort into your work","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-hard-working.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/3dfca8fa63ad.mp3"},{"en":"patient","pos":"adj","ru":"терпеливый","kk":"шыдамды","def":"able to wait, or to deal with problems, calmly","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-patient.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/b1b0b8de8a62.mp3"},{"en":"creative","pos":"adj","ru":"творческий","kk":"шығармашыл","def":"good at producing new ideas","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-creative.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/df0b6c410fc7.mp3"},{"en":"honest","pos":"adj","ru":"честный","kk":"адал","def":"always telling the truth and never cheating","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-honest.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/53861851a146.mp3"},{"en":"smart","pos":"adj","ru":"умный, сообразительный","kk":"ақылды","def":"intelligent and quick to understand","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-smart.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/155635568414.mp3"},{"en":"stupid","pos":"adj","ru":"глупый","kk":"ақымақ","def":"showing very little intelligence or thought","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-stupid.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/5514ae81cf9b.mp3"},{"en":"romantic","pos":"adj","ru":"романтичный","kk":"романтикалы","def":"showing strong feelings of love","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-romantic.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/346f5986a97e.mp3"},{"en":"extrovert","pos":"n","ru":"экстраверт","kk":"экстраверт","def":"a person who is happiest with other people and says what they think openly","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-extrovert.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/837e54588084.mp3"},{"en":"introvert","pos":"n","ru":"интроверт","kk":"интроверт","def":"a person who prefers quiet and time alone, and thinks before speaking","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-introvert.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/5a8c95b2a837.mp3"},{"en":"characteristic","pos":"n","ru":"черта характера","kk":"мінез ерекшелігі","def":"a quality that is typical of a particular person or thing","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-characteristic.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/8c7d515fba67.mp3"},{"en":"best-selling","pos":"adj","ru":"бестселлерный","kk":"бестселлер атанған","def":"sold in very large numbers","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-best-selling.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/249693897d29.mp3"},{"en":"fair","pos":"adj","ru":"справедливый","kk":"әділ","def":"treating everyone equally and in a reasonable way","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-fair.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/187770cf5af2.mp3"},{"en":"similar","pos":"adj","ru":"похожий","kk":"ұқсас","def":"almost the same, but not exactly","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-similar.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/af62f3021051.mp3"},{"en":"different","pos":"adj","ru":"другой, непохожий","kk":"өзгеше","def":"not the same","img":"/course/a2/img/l16-different.webp","audio":"/learning/audio/a2/517d5a724086.mp3"}]},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"confident","options":["уверенный в себе","застенчивый","общительный","дружелюбный","трудолюбивый"],"answer":"уверенный в себе","optionsKk":["өзіне сенімді","ұялшақ","көпшіл","достық ниетті","еңбекқор"],"answerKk":"өзіне сенімді"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"shy","options":["застенчивый","творческий","честный","умный, сообразительный","глупый"],"answer":"застенчивый","optionsKk":["ұялшақ","шығармашыл","адал","ақылды","ақымақ"],"answerKk":"ұялшақ"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"sociable","options":["общительный","экстраверт","интроверт","черта характера","бестселлерный"],"answer":"общительный","optionsKk":["көпшіл","экстраверт","интроверт","мінез ерекшелігі","бестселлер атанған"],"answerKk":"көпшіл"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"friendly","options":["дружелюбный","похожий","другой, непохожий","трудолюбивый","терпеливый"],"answer":"дружелюбный","optionsKk":["достық ниетті","ұқсас","өзгеше","еңбекқор","шыдамды"],"answerKk":"достық ниетті"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"hard-working","options":["трудолюбивый","умный, сообразительный","глупый","романтичный","экстраверт"],"answer":"трудолюбивый","optionsKk":["еңбекқор","ақылды","ақымақ","романтикалы","экстраверт"],"answerKk":"еңбекқор"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"patient","options":["терпеливый","бестселлерный","справедливый","похожий","другой, непохожий"],"answer":"терпеливый","optionsKk":["шыдамды","бестселлер атанған","әділ","ұқсас","өзгеше"],"answerKk":"шыдамды"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"<p class=\"s-en\">My sister&rsquo;s <b>cleverer than</b> me.</p><p class=\"s-note\" data-t=\"sy014\">Short adjective &rarr; <b>-er</b> + <b>than</b>. <i>than</i> is weak here: it sounds like <i>&thinsp;th&rsquo;n</i>.</p>"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"<p class=\"s-en\">My brother <b>isn&rsquo;t as confident as</b> my sister.</p><p class=\"s-note\"><b>as &hellip; as</b> = the same amount. With <i>not</i>, it means less.</p>"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"<p class=\"s-en\">I&rsquo;m <b>taller than</b> my parents.</p><p class=\"s-note\">One syllable &rarr; <b>-er</b>. Never <i>more tall</i>.</p>"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"","prompt":"Which sentence compares one thing with all the others?","options":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"answer":"Sentence 4"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"Listen. Which sentence do you hear?","prompt":"Play","options":["My sister’s cleverer than me.","My sister’s as clever as me.","neither of these"],"answer":"My sister’s cleverer than me."},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"My brother is ____ than me.","options":["taller","more tall","neither of these"],"answer":"taller"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"This is ____ book in the library.","options":["the most interesting","the interestingest","neither of these"],"answer":"the most interesting"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"She’s ____ than her sister.","options":["more confident","confidenter","neither of these"],"answer":"more confident"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"Today is ____ than yesterday.","options":["better","gooder","neither of these"],"answer":"better"},{"stage":"Listening","type":"listen","title":"","prompt":"Before you read. Look at the title. Who do you think “the quiet ones” are?","options":["people who work in libraries","people who prefer to listen rather than talk","people who are unfriendly"],"answer":"people who prefer to listen rather than talk","track":"Track_6.1.mp3"},{"stage":"Listening","type":"rows","title":"Read again. True or false?","sub":"","track":"Track_6.1.mp3","items":[{"q":"Extroverts usually think before they speak.","options":["True","False","The text does not say"],"answer":"False"},{"q":"For a long time, schools gave more attention to confident students.","options":["True","False","The text does not say"],"answer":"True"}]},{"stage":"Speaking","type":"write","title":"Talk about it.","sub":"Напиши ответ, затем проверь себя","placeholder":"Твой ответ…","model":"… is much / a bit more patient than …"},{"stage":"Wrap","type":"checklist","title":"Отметь, чему научился","sub":"Я могу…","items":["compare two people or things — quieter than, more confident than","say two people are the same — as hard-working as","say who is above all the others — the most creative, the best","say how big the difference is — much quieter, a bit more patient","describe someone’s character — shy, sociable, patient, honest, creative","talk about quantity recycled · Lesson 14 — much, many, a few, a little, enough"]}]}